# Panzanella

Based on [https://www.themediterraneandish.com/…](https://www.themediterraneandish.com/tomato-panzanella-salad-recipe/#wprm-recipe-container-34832) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251111231318/https://www.themediterraneandish.com/tomato-panzanella-salad-recipe/))

{ rating="5" image="panzanella.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] [Rustic Baguette]{ ing="rustic-baguette" } or 1/2 loaf Italian bread or Ciabatta, cut into 1” cubes
- [ ] 1.5 lbs [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }, cubed
- [ ] [Salt and Pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/8 cup Extra [virgin olive oil]{ ing="virgin-olive-oil" }
- [ ] 1/8 cup [red wine vinegar]{ ing="red-wine-vinegar" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [Dijon mustard]{ ing="dijon-mustard" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [Dried Thyme]{ ing="dried-thyme" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [Dried Basil]{ ing="dried-basil" } or 1/2 cup fresh
- [ ] 2 [garlic cloves]{ ing="garlic-cloves" }, minced
- [ ] 4 oz fresh [baby mozzarella]{ ing="baby-mozzarella" }
- [ ] (Optional) 2 [Shallots]{ ing="shallots" }, peeled and thinly sliced
- [ ] (Optional) 1 cup [white beans]{ ing="white-beans" }, such as Peruvian or Navy
- [ ] (Optional) [Spinach]{ ing="spinach" }

## Recipe

1. Toast the bread: Pre-heat oven to 400F

   1. In a large mixing bowl, toss the bread cubes, 1/2 tsp salt, 1 tsp [thyme]{ ing="dried-thyme" }, and a generous drizzle of [olive oil]{ ing="virgin-olive-oil" }. Save the bowl
   1. Spread bread cubes on a sheet pan in a single layer. Bake for 10 min until golden and crispy, then let cool
1. Prepare [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }: In a colander over the large bowl, toss the tomatoes with 1 tsp salt, 1 tsp [basil]{ ing="dried-basil" }, and 1 tsp thyme. Allow to drain for a few minutes to release juices
1. Make dressing: Set the colander aside. With the tomato juice in the bowl, add the [red wine vinegar]{ ing="red-wine-vinegar" }, olive oil, [dijon mustard]{ ing="dijon-mustard" }, 1 tsp thyme, 1 tsp basil, [garlic cloves]{ ing="garlic-cloves" }, and black [pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }. Whisk to combine
1. Assemble: In the bowl, combine toasted bread, tomatoes, [mozzarella]{ ing="baby-mozzarella" }, optional [shallots]{ ing="shallots" }, [beans]{ ing="white-beans" }, and [spinach]{ ing="spinach" }. Pour dressing over and toss to coat. Let sit for 20-30 minutes to allow bread to absorb flavors

## Notes

1. Best served within 1-2 hours to maintain some bread texture. For longer storage, keep bread separate until serving
1. For extra flavor: Add capers, kalamata olives, or anchovies
1. Healthier option: Use whole grain bread and add more greens like arugula or spinach
1. Serves 4-6 as a side dish
